WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:10.520
Hey, welcome back to 40 Days of Holiness. Grab your workbook.

2
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:14.480
Today we are in Psalm 86:11. All right,

3
00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:18.370
we're reading David's words in Psalm 86:11, where he says,

4
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:22.560
"Teach me your way, Lord, that I may rely on your faithfulness.

5
00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:26.940
Give me an undivided heart that I may

6
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.720
fear your name." Now the same word is used in 1

7
00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:34.600
Chronicles 12:38, where it said, "All these men who

8
00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:37.120
were fighting men volunteered to serve in the ranks.

9
00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:40.990
They came to Hebron fully determined to make David king over

10
00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:44.640
all Israel. And all the rest of the Israelites were also

11
00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:48.340
of echad, they were of one mind to make

12
00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:51.820
David king." So that's what it means,

13
00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:55.600
undivided, united, whole. Now, in this

14
00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:57.680
passage, I want you to notice four things.

15
00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:01.940
I want you to notice that number one, David saw something in himself by the

16
00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:05.500
insight the Holy Spirit gave him. You see that?

17
00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:08.790
He saw, he realized that his heart was divided.

18
00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:12.820
Now this picture of the heart is consistent with the rest of scripture.

19
00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:16.600
When we are unsaved, we are people of one nature,

20
00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:22.060
not able to do anything but evil. But when we are saved, we're raised to

21
00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:25.760
new life in Christ, we have the Holy Spirit living within us, and we become

22
00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:29.260
people of coexisting natures, a regenerated

23
00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:33.420
nature of spiritual life, a nature of sin that will

24
00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:36.440
unfailingly lead us towards sin and death.

25
00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:40.720
And when our heart is divided, it prevents us from consistently

26
00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:43.920
living in the fear of the Lord. That's what David says here.

27
00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:47.780
And that matters because Proverbs teaches us that by

28
00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:51.080
the fear of the Lord, men depart from evil. Right?

29
00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:55.040
So it's going to be hard to depart from evil as long as you don't have the fear of

30
00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:59.000
the Lord, and it's hard to have the fear of the Lord if you

31
00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:03.040
have a divided heart. Now I want you to notice that

32
00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:06.620
before you are saved, you don't have a divided heart.

33
00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:09.039
It is united in the wrong direction.

34
00:02:09.961 --> 00:02:13.940
But once you know the Lord, you have a heart that is divided.

35
00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:18.520
Now, I hope in the last few days the Lord has helped you to see this like

36
00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:20.060
he did David. All right? Number two,

37
00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:24.720
David was drawn by the Holy Spirit to pray this division

38
00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:28.500
would be healed by God's power. I just want to point out this wasn't David

39
00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:32.380
being overly dramatic or asking for something that wasn't

40
00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:35.380
the Lord's will. This is the Holy Spirit. This is scripture.

41
00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:39.920
The Holy Spirit inspired David to ask

42
00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:40.220
this.

43
00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:43.520
He's the one who put these words in David's mouth.

44
00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:45.910
Again, possibility glasses, right?

45
00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:49.170
If the Holy Spirit inspired David to ask this,

46
00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:51.940
wouldn't he also do the same for you?

47
00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:55.780
Wouldn't he inspire you to ask that your heart also

48
00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:57.700
would be undivided?

49
00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:01.440
David was implicitly trusting God.

50
00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:05.020
Number three, David was implicitly trusting God to do what he asked.

51
00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:09.300
And number four, David knew this united heart would

52
00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:12.600
produce a heart and behavioral change.

53
00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:15.800
It would make him fear the Lord more consistently.

54
00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:16.720
Now,

55
00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:21.580
here's the question. As a believer, can you do any less than

56
00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:25.549
David did? And is God any less willing to do

57
00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:27.060
it now than he was back then?

58
00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:31.820
So today's metaphor is from a divided heart to a

59
00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:35.700
united heart, leading to a changed attitude of fear of the Lord and

60
00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:38.400
power to live in victory. That's holiness.

61
00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:42.900
So as we seek the Lord, the first thing I want to tell you is that we

62
00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:45.980
talked about loving God with all of your heart yesterday.

63
00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:47.660
And now we're talking about

64
00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:52.680
that David's saying, "I want the Lord to unite my heart,"

65
00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:56.260
because he recognizes the division in his heart.

66
00:03:56.860 --> 00:04:00.850
And if that's the case, then if you've seen the same thing, how does

67
00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:04.470
God heal it? Yesterday we were going to start talking about how God does

68
00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:08.390
this. How does he go about it? Well, the metaphor here is that

69
00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:10.540
God says you've got a divided heart.

70
00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:14.540
I can't help you love the Lord your God with all your heart as long as your

71
00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:18.500
heart is divided. You're going to need to ask him to unite your heart.

72
00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:23.120
You're going to need to pray and begin seeking the Lord and saying, "Lord, I want

73
00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:26.920
my heart to be undivided. I want it to be one

74
00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:29.860
so that I can adequately fear your name."

75
00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:34.480
So let's look at tomorrow. We will be continuing on. All right?

76
00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:38.450
And I just want to encourage you, don't give up. Don't quit. Start asking.

77
00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:41.120
Today's the day. Start asking. Start seeking.

78
00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:44.720
"Lord, I want that division healed." Maybe you used to think it wasn't possible.

79
00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:48.260
Maybe you used to think this is something I just have to live with till I get to

80
00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:48.600
heaven.

81
00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:50.180
But I'm telling you

82
00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:52.580
that the Bible's saying something different.

83
00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:57.000
That when the Holy Spirit inspired and put these words into David's

84
00:04:57.040 --> 00:05:00.940
heart, he was showing him what he could do, not

85
00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:03.740
something he had to live with and someday he was going to give him an undivided

86
00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:07.690
heart when he got to heaven. But I believe that the Holy Spirit is able to give you

87
00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:11.160
an undivided heart now by the power of grace. All right?

88
00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:15.480
So we'll keep talking about tomorrow. For right now, let's do our workbook.

89
00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:17.690
Let's meditate on things, and I'll see you tomorrow.
